## Guidelines:
0. **Only these packages are ever installed — this applies to EVERY call, not just the one generating package.json**: `next`, `react`, `react-dom`, `next/link`, `next/image`, `next/navigation` (all part of `next`), plus Node/React/TypeScript built-ins. Do NOT `import` from any other npm package (no `tailwind-merge`, `clsx`, `date-fns`, `uuid`, icon libraries, form libraries, animation libraries, or anything else) — it will not be installed and the build will fail with "Module not found", exactly like a missing local file would. If you want conditional/merged Tailwind classes, write a tiny local helper inline (e.g. `const cx = (...c: (string | false | undefined)[]) => c.filter(Boolean).join(' ')`) instead of importing one from npm. If you want an icon, use inline SVG markup, not an icon package.
1. **Stay in scope**: only return files for what "Your scope for this call" above describes — either the one target page, or the shared/root files. Other parallel calls handle the rest; returning files outside your scope will overwrite or conflict with their output when everything is merged.
2. **First pass (PriorFiles empty)**: Generate your scope's complete file(s) from Spec + DesignTokens.
3. **Retry pass (PriorFiles + QAFeedback set)**: PriorFiles includes the FULL app (all pages + shared files, for context/consistency) — but still return ONLY your own scope's file(s), updated to fix whatever QA flagged that falls within your scope. If QA feedback doesn't mention any file in your scope, return your scope's files unchanged.
4. **Enforce max total size**: ~500KB of source code max for this call's output.
5. **App Router structure**: Use `src/app/` with `layout.tsx`, `page.tsx`, `globals.css`.
6. **Tailwind**: Use design tokens via `theme.extend` in tailwind.config.ts or CSS variables in globals.css.
7. **TypeScript**: Strict mode, proper types for props and data.
7a. **Server vs Client Components (App Router — get this right, it's a hard build failure, not a warning)**: every component/page is a Server Component by default and CANNOT use React hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useRef`, `useContext`, etc.), browser-only APIs, or event handler props (`onClick`, `onChange`, `onSubmit`, ...). If a file uses ANY of those, its very first line — before imports, before anything else — MUST be `"use client"` on its own line. Forgetting this fails the build with "You're importing a component that needs useState/useEffect/... It only works in a Client Component". When in doubt about whether a component needs interactivity (forms, toggles, carousels, anything with state or handlers), add `"use client"`.
8. **Accessibility**: Semantic HTML, alt text, proper heading hierarchy, focus states.
9. **PWA**: If kind=pwa and you're generating shared/root files, manifest.json + sw.js are HARD REQUIREMENTS.
10. Output MUST use the `>>>FILE: <path>` / `>>>ENDFILE` delimited format above, containing ONLY the files in your scope.